{"page_content": "ACME/Flame Design Final Report (2023) \n \n6 April 2023 \n30 \n \n \nSoFIE \nSolid Fuel Ignition and Extinction (project to follow ACME in the CIR facility) \nSORD \nScience Operations Requirements Document (an ACME supplement to the ISRD) \nSRD \nScience Requirements Document \nT/C (or t/c) \nThermocouple \nTDRS \nTracking and Data Relay Satellite (System) \nTFP \nThin Filament Pyrometry (a method for gas-phase temperature measurements) \nTIFF or TIF \nTagged Image File Format (e.g., for the CFI intensified, HiBMs, and LLL-UV cameras) \nTM \nthermistor \nTS \nTransport Stream (a video format) \nTSC \nTelescience Support Center (also known as the GIPOC) \nUV \nultraviolet \nZe \nZeldovich number \nzero-g \nzero gravity, i.e., microgravity \nZIN \nZIN Technologies, Inc. (ACME engineering and operations provider) \n\u00b5A \nmicroamp \n \nWhile this list of abbreviations and acronyms is long, it is not comprehensive.  Contact ACME Project \nScientist Dennis Stocker (216-433-2166, dennis.p.stocker@nasa.gov) for additional clarification.", "metadata": {"source": "PSI-10_Reports_FinalRpt_ACMEFlameDesign.pdf", "page": 30}}